   "response_text": "All 119 parser/option tests pass.\n\n**Root cause:** In `src/click/parser.py`, `_process_opts` split the long option argument with `arg.split(\"=\")[:2]`. That splits on *every* equals sign and keeps only the first two pieces, so `--name=a=b=c` gave `explicit_value=\"a\"` \u2014 everything after the second `=` was thrown away.\n\n**Fix:** `arg.split(\"=\", 1)` \u2014 split only on the first equals, so the entire remainder (`a=b=c`) becomes the value.\n\n- `--name=a=b=c` \u2192 `'a=b=c'` \u2705\n- `--name a=b=c` \u2192 `'a=b=c'` \u2705 (unchanged, already correct)\n- Full corpus: 119 parser/option tests green.\n\nDONE",
